Subject: libsmbclient: read vendor, run, and etc smb.conf tiers

Source: Nex
Upstream: not submitted; this narrows the Nex UAPI tiering rule to the
libsmbclient context init path only, rather than samba's shared
lp_load() used by every samba program

smbc_init_context() (via SMBC_module_init()) already looks for the
user's $HOME/.smb/smb.conf before falling back to the single compiled
get_dyn_CONFIGFILE(), which this manifest's --sysconfdir=/etc build
resolves to /etc/samba/smb.conf. That fallback has no vendor default
and no per-boot override, so a Nex deployment cannot ship a client
default such as a workgroup and a boot cannot override it.

This patch keeps get_dyn_CONFIGFILE() (/etc/samba/smb.conf) exactly
where it is and adds two lower tiers read before it:

  1. /usr/lib/samba/smb.conf, the package/assembly vendor default.
     This manifest already installs its private libraries below
     /usr/lib/samba, so the vendor config lives beside them.
  2. /run/samba/smb.conf, a boot-time override.

The three tiers are merged, not selected: lp_load_client() on the
vendor file resets every global to its compiled default and then
applies whatever the vendor file sets, establishing the baseline.
lp_load_client_no_reinit() on the /run and /etc files does not reset
globals first, so it only overwrites the parameters each file actually
names and leaves every other parameter at whatever the lower tier (or
the compiled default) already set. That is the same overlay upstream
already uses a few lines below for $HOME/.smb/smb.conf.append, so a
partial administrator file cannot blank out a vendor default the way a
plain reinit-and-reload would. A missing file at any tier makes that
tier's pm_process() fail and leaves the previous tier's values
untouched, so a missing vendor or /run file is silent.

The $HOME/.smb/smb.conf and $HOME/.smb/smb.conf.append behavior is
unchanged: a readable user file still replaces the whole system lookup,
and the append file still overlays on top of whichever system tier
loaded.

This patch touches only source3/libsmb/libsmb_context.c, the
libsmbclient-specific context bootstrap. It does not touch
source3/param/loadparm.c or dynconfig, so smbd, nmbd, winbindd, and
every other samba program this manifest does not build are unaffected.

--- a/source3/libsmb/libsmb_context.c
+++ b/source3/libsmb/libsmb_context.c
@@ -37,0 +38,11 @@
+ * Nex UAPI tiering for the libsmbclient-only system config lookup.
+ * get_dyn_CONFIGFILE() (/etc/samba/smb.conf under this build) stays the
+ * administrator tier. These two lower tiers are read before it: a vendor
+ * default below /usr, which this package already uses for its private
+ * libraries, and a /run override for a boot-time default. See
+ * SMBC_module_init() below for how the three are merged.
+ */
+#define NEX_SMB_CONF_VENDOR "/usr/lib/samba/smb.conf"
+#define NEX_SMB_CONF_RUN "/run/samba/smb.conf"
+
+/*
@@ -72,0 +84,2 @@
+		bool sys_loaded;
+
@@ -74,4 +87,17 @@
-		 * Well, if that failed, try the get_dyn_CONFIGFILE
-		 * Which points to the standard locn, and if that
-		 * fails, silently ignore it and use the internal
-		 * defaults ...
+		 * No per-user config. Build the system configuration from
+		 * three tiers, lowest priority first, each overlaying only
+		 * the parameters it actually sets:
+		 *
+		 *   1. NEX_SMB_CONF_VENDOR under /usr, the package or
+		 *      assembly default.
+		 *   2. NEX_SMB_CONF_RUN under /run, a boot-time override.
+		 *   3. get_dyn_CONFIGFILE() under /etc, the administrator
+		 *      file, unchanged from upstream.
+		 *
+		 * lp_load_client() resets every global to its compiled
+		 * default before parsing, so it establishes the baseline.
+		 * lp_load_client_no_reinit() leaves whatever is already set
+		 * and only overwrites the parameters the file names, the
+		 * same overlay used below for smb.conf.append. A missing
+		 * file at any tier is silent: that tier's pm_process() fails
+		 * and the previous tier's values are untouched.
@@ -80 +106,13 @@
-		if (!lp_load_client(get_dyn_CONFIGFILE())) {
+		sys_loaded = lp_load_client(NEX_SMB_CONF_VENDOR);
+		if (!sys_loaded) {
+			DEBUG(5, ("Could not load config file: %s\n",
+				  NEX_SMB_CONF_VENDOR));
+		}
+
+		if (lp_load_client_no_reinit(NEX_SMB_CONF_RUN)) {
+			sys_loaded = True;
+		}
+
+		if (lp_load_client_no_reinit(get_dyn_CONFIGFILE())) {
+			sys_loaded = True;
+		} else {
